Tasks: Marca de la celda de origen (FR12) and Destello de la celda de destino
(FR13, FR14) (Fase 5, pattern-copy_20260910)

Both signals in one commit: they share the cell body and the same new constants,
and neither compiles usefully without the other's plumbing.

- **The origin mark is a filled block in the top-trailing corner**, off-white,
  `Brutalist.copyMark`. Not a border: `playing`, `queued` and the selected cell
  already share the three borders, and a fourth would not be distinguishable at
  a metre. It is drawn only while looking at its own Bank — `copiedSlotIndex`
  asks `PatternClipboard.markedSlot(inBank:)` — so in another Bank there is no
  cell to mark and the signal is simply that `paste` is enabled.
- **The destination cell flashes** on paste and on a chord copy, whether or not
  it held material (FR13, FR14). One ease-out fade, nothing hung off the clock:
  no per-frame work and no dependence on the transport running. Setting the flash
  and animating it away are separated by a hop to the next turn of the loop —
  in the same pass SwiftUI collapses them and nothing shows.
- `pasteDestinationIndex` on the model tells the view which cell will receive,
  because running it is not the selected one. The destination is read *before*
  pasting: what flashes is the cell that received, not the one that would
  receive next.
- The mark is hidden from VoiceOver as a shape but the cell's label says
  "copied", so the state is not visual-only.

